In terms of behavior, the Yellow-breasted Chat is known for its complex and varied song, often described as a series of whistles, trills, and chattering sounds. It is also known to mimic the calls of other birds and even human speech. This mimicking ability is one of its unique identifying traits.

The Yellow-breasted Chat is found in North America, primarily in the eastern United States and southern Canada. It inhabits a variety of habitats including deciduous forests, shrublands, and urban areas. The bird is typically seen perched on branches or wires, often in open areas within its forest habitat.
